-- Run this once in the Supabase SQL editor for project ucvsnxexmvxpccyatmmk.
-- Backfills make/model on the dealership's `vehicles` stock catalog from
-- display_name, for every row where make/model were never filled in.
--
-- These are GTA Online's in-fiction vehicle manufacturers (Vapid, Declasse,
-- Pegassi, etc, plus a couple of real-world brands the server added as-is --
-- McLaren, Bugatti), not real-world car brands. Every split was either a
-- direct manufacturer-name match, or confirmed against another row in this
-- same catalogue that already carries the full 'Manufacturer Model' name for
-- the same model (e.g. 'Karin Asterope' confirms 'Asterope GZ' is a Karin).
-- Generated from a one-off script, not hand-typed -- see the scratchpad
-- vehicle_make_model_stage*.py files this was built from.
--
-- A handful of rows were left with make/model still NULL rather than
-- guessed -- generic/unbranded vehicles (Tractor, Forklift, Trailer, Tow
-- Truck, Lawn Mower, etc) or names with no manufacturer I could confidently
-- identify (Hardy, Aleutian, Woodlander, Starlight, Minimus, Ronin, FR36,
-- Marelle, Boxboy, Mogul RS, Desert Raid, Bordeaux Hauler, MCH Shuttlebus,
-- 'Something Something JCB' -- this last one reads like an unfinished
-- placeholder name, worth a look). Matches this app's 'unknown stays NULL,
-- never guessed' convention.
--
-- 3 rows were resolved to a MAJORITY pick despite a real alternate candidate
-- existing elsewhere in this catalogue -- flagged individually below and in
-- the chat report, not silently decided.

